    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "In the force-current analogy, force corresponds to current, and displacement corresponds to flux. However, in mechanical-electrical analogies, there are two common analogies: force-voltage and force-current. In the force-current analogy (also called the mobility analogy), displacement (x) maps to flux linkage (\u03bb), and since flux linkage is the integral of voltage over time, the analogous quantity to displacement is **flux** (or flux linkage). Among the given options, **flux** is listed as option I.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{I}\n$$",
