    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A flat key mounted on a motor shaft 4 in. diameter is subjected to a maximum twisting moment of 45,000 lbs-in. Design a suitable key assuming the design stress in bearing to be 24,000 psi and in shear at 9000 psi.\n\nOptions: \nA. thickness = 7/8 in. width = 1.5 in. length = 3 in.\nB. thickness = 1 in. width = 2 in. length = 1.5 in.\nC. thickness = 3/4 in. width = 1 in. length = 2.5 in.\nD. thickness = 7/8 in. width = 1.25 in. length = 2.5 in.\nE. thickness = 1 in. width = 1.5 in. length = 2 in.\nF. thickness = 1/2 in. width = 0.75 in. length = 3 in.\nG. thickness = 5/8 in. width = 1.25 in. length = 2 in.\nH. thickness = 1/2 in. width = 1.25 in. length = 1.5 in.\nI. thickness = 1/2 in. width = 1 in. length = 2.5 in.\nJ. thickness = 3/4 in. width = 1.5 in. length = 3.5 in.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To determine the correct key size, both shear and bearing stresses must be checked. The torque is 45,000 lb-in, shaft diameter is 4 in, so the radius is 2 in; force on the key = Torque / radius = 22,500 lb. For shear stress: \u03c4 = F / (w \u00d7 L) \u2264 9000 psi \u2192 w\u00d7L \u2265 22,500 / 9000 = 2.5 in\u00b2. For bearing stress: \u03c3 = F / (t/2 \u00d7 L) \u2264 24,000 psi (since t/2 is the bearing area depth) \u2192 (t \u00d7 L)/2 \u2265 22,500 / 24,000 = 0.9375 \u2192 t\u00d7L \u2265 1.875 in\u00b2. Checking options, only C (t=0.75, w=1, L=2.5) gives w\u00d7L = 2.5 \u2265 2.5 and t\u00d7L = 1.875 \u2265 1.875 \u2014 exactly meeting both criteria.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
