 a-c voltage = 150 volts; 2(b) alternating current = 14 amp, direct current = 9 amp\nI. 1(a) d-c voltage = 295 volts, d-c current = 5.08 amp; 1(b) a-c input current = 7.5 amp; 2(a) a-c voltage = 140 volts; 2(b) alternating current = 17.86 amp, direct current = 11.9 amp\nJ. 1(a) d-c voltage = 330 volts, d-c current = 4.55 amp; 1(b) a-c input current = 6.35 amp; 2(a) a-c voltage = 220 volts; 2(b) alternating current = 11.36 amp, direct current = 7.58 amp\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For question (1), with 1.5 kW at 230 V AC and unity power factor, the AC input current is $ I = \\frac{1500}{230} \\approx 6.52 $ A, closest to 6.5 A. The DC output power equals input, so for typical full-wave rectification, average DC voltage is about $ V_{dc} \\approx 0.9 \\times 230 = 207 $ V, but considering peak voltage $ V_{dc} \\approx \\sqrt{2} \\times 230 \\approx 325 $ V for unfiltered output, matching closer to option G. For (2), inverting 2.5 kW at 230 V DC gives AC power; $ I_{dc} = \\frac{2500}{230} \\approx 10.87 $ A, and AC voltage should be near $ \\frac{2500}{I_{ac}} $; option G matches closely with consistent values.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
