      "generated_answer": "The characteristic equation is $ r^2 - \\frac{5}{6}r + \\frac{1}{6} = 0 $, with roots $ r = \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{1}{3} $.  \nThus, the impulse response has the form $ h[n] = A\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n u[n] + B\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^n u[n] $.  \nUsing initial conditions $ h[-1] = 0 $ and solving for $ h[0] = 1 $, $ h[1] = \\frac{5}{6} $, we find $ A = 3 $, $ B = -2 $, so $ h[n] = 3\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n u[n] - 2\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^n u[n] $, which matches option **E**.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
