      "generated_answer": "The particular solution for the input $3^n$ is of the form $y_p[n] = A \\cdot 3^n$. Substituting into the difference equation yields $A = \\frac{27}{20}$. The homogeneous solution solves $y_h[n] - \\frac{5}{6}y_h[n-1] + \\frac{1}{6}y_h[n-2] = 0$, giving roots $\\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\frac{1}{3}$, so $y_h[n] = C_1 \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n + C_2 \\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)^n$. Applying initial conditions $y[-1] = y[-2] = 0$ confirms the constants match option C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
