      "generated_answer": "The torque transmitted is 60 ft-lb = 720 in-lb. This torque is resisted by 4 bolts on a 3 in. bolt circle, so the force per bolt is $ F = \\frac{T}{r \\cdot n} = \\frac{720}{(1.5) \\cdot 4} = 120 $ lb. Using shear stress $ \\tau = \\frac{F}{A} $, solving for area $ A = \\frac{F}{\\tau} = \\frac{120}{10000} = 0.012 \\, \\text{in}^2 $, then bolt diameter $ d = \\sqrt{\\frac{4A}{\\pi}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{4 \\cdot 0.012}{\\pi}} \\approx 0.1236 $ in.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
