      "generated_answer": "The output power is 100 kW. Total losses include copper losses (armature, series, and shunt fields), rotational losses (3840 W), and stray-load loss (1% of 100 kW = 1000 W). Calculating armature current as 400 A (100,000 / 250), armature copper loss is $ I_a^2 R_a = (400)^2 \\times 0.012 = 1920 $ W; series and commutating pole losses are each $ (400)^2 \\times 0.004 = 640 $ W; shunt field loss is $ 250 \\times 2.6 = 650 $ W. Total losses sum to 1920 + 640 + 640 + 650 + 3840 + 1000 = 8690 W. Efficiency is $ 100,000 / (100,000 + 8690) \\approx 0.920 $, closest to 0.915.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
