    "global index": "MMLUPro_health_5313",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A teacher sets up a reward system for her elementary school students. At the end of each day, she gives a sticker to each student who showed up on time that morning. At the end of each week, she gives a sticker to any student who got above a 90% on three quizzes in a row. After months of this regimen, she finds that performance on the quizzes has increased significantly but that tardiness has only decreased slightly. Which of the following best explains the teacher\u2019s observation?\n\nOptions: \nA. The students had more intrinsic motivation to do well on quizzes than to show up on time.\nB. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a variable-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nC. The students were more excited about the quizzes than about the reward system.\nD. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a variable-interval schedule than it was to a fixed-ratio schedule.\nE. Variable ratio schedules create the strongest responses and behavior that is the least susceptible to extinction.\nF. The students\u2019 behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nG. The students' behavior change was weaker in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nH. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-interval schedule than it was to a continuous reinforcement schedule.\nI. The students' behavior change was stronger in response to a continuous reinforcement schedule than it was to a variable-ratio schedule.\nJ. The students\u2019 behavior change was stronger in response to a fixed-ratio schedule than it was to a variable-interval schedule.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The daily attendance reward is a continuous reinforcement schedule (every on-time arrival gets a sticker), while the weekly quiz reward is a fixed-ratio schedule (a sticker after every three high quiz scores). Fixed-ratio schedules typically produce strong, consistent responses because the reward is predictable after a set number of behaviors. This explains why quiz performance improved more than punctuality, as fixed-ratio reinforcement is often more effective than continuous reinforcement for building sustained effort.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
