    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The patient presents with acute limb ischemia following recent femoral-popliteal bypass, evidenced by sudden onset of foot pain, pallor, coolness, and loss of distal pulses despite a patent proximal pulse. This clinical picture suggests acute graft thrombosis, which is a surgical emergency requiring immediate restoration of blood flow to prevent limb loss. The most appropriate management is immediate surgical exploration to identify and correct the cause of occlusion.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
