      "generated_answer": "The products of protein digestion are primarily absorbed in the small intestine either as free amino acids or as di- and tripeptides, which are then further broken down inside the enterocytes. Option A correctly describes this process. The other options are incorrect: gastric chief cells secrete pepsinogen, not pancreatic enzymes like chymotrypsin; pancreatic enzymes are secreted by the pancreas and act in the lumen; and multiple amino acid transporters (more than one) exist for absorption.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
