    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The strength of a gypsum investment is dependent\non:\n\nOptions: \nA. Carbon content\nB. Silica content\nC. Gypsum\nD. Copper\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The strength of a gypsum investment is primarily dependent on its composition, particularly the gypsum (calcium sulfate dihydrate) content, which forms the matrix upon setting. While silica may be added as a refractory material to modify thermal properties or reduce shrinkage, it does not fundamentally determine the setting strength. The key structural component is gypsum itself, as the setting reaction involves rehydration and crystal interlocking of calcium sulfate hemihydrate to form dihydrate.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
