    "global index": "MedMCQA_605",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sending the parents outside the operatory and threatening the child that they won't be back until he stops crying-is an example of which of the following behavior management techniques:\n\nOptions: \nA. Omission\nB. Negative reinforcement\nC. Positive reinforcement\nD. Modelling\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The described technique involves removing the parent (a preferred stimulus) contingent on crying, which reduces the crying behavior by avoiding the unpleasant consequence of parental absence. This aligns with **negative reinforcement**, as the removal of the aversive condition (parent being outside) reinforces the cessation of crying\u2014though commonly confused with punishment, here it functions to increase non-crying behavior via relief from separation. However, since threatening removal *decreases* crying through punishment (not reinforcement), the best fit is actually **A. Omission**, a form of negative punishment where a desired stimulus (parent\u2019s presence) is withheld to reduce behavior.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
