    "global index": "MedMCQA_1446",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Sequential arrangement question on JVP. Staing with \"a\" wave. A-First hea sound B-T wave C-R wave D-Rapid ejection phase\n\nOptions: \nA. A,B,C,D\nB. A,C,D,B\nC. C,A,D,B\nD. D,C,B,A\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The JVP waveform starts with the **a wave**, which corresponds to atrial contraction and occurs just before the **first heart sound (S1)**. The **R wave** of the ECG marks ventricular depolarization and coincides with the **rapid ejection phase** of systole. The **T wave** represents ventricular repolarization and occurs later, during diastole.\n\nThus, the correct sequential order is:  \n**a wave \u2192 first heart sound (S1) \u2192 R wave \u2192 rapid ejection phase \u2192 T wave**, but since the question asks for the sequence *starting with the a wave* and lists only four items (A\u2013D), and considering timing:  \n- a wave \u2192 S1 (A)  \n- R wave (C) typically overlaps the peak of the **a** or **c** wave but precedes ejection  \n- Rapid ejection phase (D) follows R wave  \n- T wave (B) occurs after systole, after ejection  \n\nHowever, in standard JVP correlation:  \n- **a** wave \u2192 just before S1  \n- **c** wave (not listed) follows S1  \n- **v** wave (not listed) precedes S2  \nBut among given options, **R wave** correlates with onset of ventricular systole and **rapid ejection**, while **T wave** is late. The best match is:  \n**a wave \u2192 first heart sound (A) \u2192 R wave (C) \u2192 rapid ejection (D) \u2192 T wave (B)**, i.e., **A, C, D, B**.\n\n$$\n\\boxed{B}\n$$",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 169,
        "output_tokens": 342,
