      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}  \nYes, outcome can be predicted: preoperative tumour visibility, postoperative cortisol/urine free cortisol levels, and histological/radiological findings significantly correlated with remission, failure, or relapse. These factors provided statistically significant predictive value (e.g., P = 0.002\u20130.048).",
