      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}  \nThe study found that existing equations (e.g., Harris-Benedict, Yang) had lower accuracy rates (37\u201370%), especially at higher BMIs, indicating poor applicability to Chinese adults across a broad BMI range. Although a new equation achieved 78\u201380% accuracy, the question asks about *current* equations, implying the pre-existing ones cited. Thus, they are generally not fully applicable.",
