      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{A}  \nYes, the study shows Ki-67 overexpression is significantly associated with worse cancer-specific and disease-free survival, and multivariate analysis confirms it as an independent prognostic factor. The meta-analysis further supports this, reporting pooled hazard ratios >2 for poor outcomes across multiple survival endpoints.",
