    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following time signatures is a compound meter?\n\nOptions: \nA. 11/8\nB. 7/4\nC. 8/8\nD. 12/16\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Compound meters have beats that divide into three equal parts, and the numerator is typically a multiple of 3 (e.g., 6, 9, 12).  \nOption D, 12/16, has a numerator of 12 (a multiple of 3), and with a denominator of 16 (a dotted quarter note beat), it implies 4 dotted quarter-note beats per measure\u2014each divisible into three eighth notes\u2014making it compound.  \nWhile 12/8 is the standard notation for compound meter, 12/16 functions identically when interpreted as 3/4 time with dotted quarters, and in practice, 12/16 is treated as compound duple (2 dotted quarter beats, each in 3 eighth-note divisions), though some may misinterpret; however, among the options, **D** is the only one that qualifies unambiguously as compound.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
