    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "On the cello and double bass, the bow is typically held with a different technique than on the violin and viola, especially in the use of the German (or \"Butler\" grip) and French bow styles. In both cello and bass playing, particularly with the German bow, the pinky finger often rests on top of the stick rather than being curled over the frog as in violin and viola. This contrasts with violin and viola bow holds, where the pinky usually curves over the top but doesn't rest flat.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
