    "global index": "MusicTheoryBench_213",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which common tones are shared between Mode V Form 3 (V3) of Messiaen's finite transposition system (as shown in the score example) and the D Phrygian scale?\n\nOptions: \nA. D, Eb, F, A\nB. F, G, A\nC. Eb, F, G, A\nD. D, Eb, G, A\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Mode V Form 3 (V3) of Messiaen\u2019s octatonic/limited transposition modes corresponds to the collection {C, D#, E, F#, G, A}. D Phrygian scale is {D, Eb, F, G, A, Bb, C}. Intersection: D, Eb, F, G, A \u2014 but wait, Mode V Form 3 is actually the fourth mode of the seventh mode of limited transposition? Clarification: Messiaen\u2019s Mode V is the intervallic pattern [2,1,2,1,2,1,2], i.e., whole\u2013half\u2013whole\u2013half..., starting at C gives {C, D, Eb, F, G, Ab, Bb, C} \u2014 yet \u201cForm 3\u201d likely refers to a specific rotation or inversion. StandardMessiaen Mode V = transposition class of the octatonic scale (half\u2013whole): e.g., {C, Db, E, F, Gb, Ab, B, C}. But commonly, Messiaen Mode V = [2,1,2,1,2,1,2] \u2192 {C, D, Eb, F, G, Ab, Bb, C}. However, Form 3 may be transposed. In many analyses, Mode V Form 3 starting at D is {D, Eb, F, G, Ab, Bb, C, D}. Intersection with D Phrygian ({D, Eb, F, G, A, Bb, C}) = D, Eb, F, G, Bb, C \u2014 but A is not in that version. Yet Option A has D, Eb, F, A \u2014 missing G, has A. Option C has Eb, F, G, A \u2014 no D. If we assume Mode V Form 3 is the *seventh* mode of the octatonic half-whole series starting at D: D, E, G, A, Bb, C, Eb, D \u2014 i.e., {D, E, G, A, Bb, C, Eb}. Then intersection with D Phrygian ({D, Eb, F, G, A, Bb, C}) = D, Eb, G, A, Bb, C. Among options, D matches D, Eb, G, A. So likely D.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
