    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Which of the following statements about harmonics and overtones is incorrect?\n\nOptions: \nA. Harmonics and overtones have the same definition, for example: the frequency of the first overtone is twice the frequency of the fundamental.\nB. The frequency of overtones and harmonics are in an integer multiple relationship with the fundamental frequency.\nC. Partial frequencies may not have an integer multiple relationship with the fundamental frequency.\nD. In instruments with clear pitch, the fundamental frequency is usually the most obvious to the ear.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
