o make donations to the Project Gutenberg Literary\nArchive Foundation, how to help produce our new eBooks, and how to\nsubscribe to our email newsletter to hear about new eBooks.\n\n\nQuestion: How does Hunca Munca pay for what she did? \n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-Next",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Hunca Munca pays for her actions by replacing what she destroyed or took with items of equal value or utility. Specifically, after stealing feathers for her own bolster, she returns with two small wooden dishes from the dollhouse kitchen as compensation. This act of restitution aligns with the moral lesson in Beatrix Potter\u2019s tale about accountability and making amends.\n\n\\boxed{\\text{She replaces what she stole by returning two small wooden dishes from the dollhouse kitchen.}}",
