    "global index": "MMLUPro_history_4763",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The Mayan king Yax Pahsaj symbolized his royalty on a stele that depicts:\n\nOptions: \nA. a series of decisive military conquests against a rival king.\nB. a depiction of him as a corn god, a symbol of fertility and prosperity.\nC. a scene of him hunting and defeating a large jaguar.\nD. an eagle, a serpent, and a jaguar, all of which were important royal animals.\nE. him receiving a crown from the Mayan god of death and rebirth.\nF. his coronation ceremony with all the Mayan gods as witnesses.\nG. a lightning bolt descending from heaven and marking him as the leader.\nH. a large sun, symbolizing his role as a son of the Sun God.\nI. the founder of the dynasty \u201cpassing him the torch.\u201d\nJ. him standing on the peak of a mountain to signify his power.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The Mayan king Yax Pahsaj is depicted on a stele receiving the symbols of kingship from a predecessor, signifying dynastic continuity. This act is best described as the founder of the dynasty \"passing him the torch.\" Such imagery emphasizes legitimacy and ancestral authority in Maya royal ideology.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
