      "generated_answer": "An absolute date specifies a particular year or range of years, such as 1492 CE, often determined through scientific methods like radiometric dating. A relative date places events in chronological order without specifying exact years, such as \"before the Bronze Age\" or \"after the eruption.\" Thus, option H correctly distinguishes absolute dates (specific years) from relative dates (chronological sequence).\n\n\\boxed{H}",
