      "generated_answer": "Huxley describes protoplasm as \"the physical basis of life\" and explains that life involves the breakdown of this substance into ordinary matter through a process tied to vitality. He emphasizes that life arises from and depends on material components, not a separate force or spiritual entity. Therefore, he views life as a property emerging from specific physical matter.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
