    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The first passage from *The Epic of Gilgamesh* describes the grim nature of the underworld, emphasizing darkness, death, and finality. The second, from *The Maxims of Ptahhotep*, reflects moral teachings grounded in divine order (ma\u2019at), linking truth and righteousness with guidance in life and implicitly in the afterlife. Both texts reflect religious worldviews centered on death, morality, and the soul\u2019s journey, making the afterlife the central theme.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
