      "generated_answer": "Kipling's poem frames imperialism as a noble duty of Western civilizations to uplift and civilize non-Western peoples, whom he describes as \"half-devil and half-child.\" He emphasizes service, sacrifice, and the moral obligation to bring order, health, and prosperity to colonized lands. This reflects a belief in the responsibility of advanced nations to guide less-developed ones, not through irony or critique, but as a solemn calling.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
