      "generated_answer": "Fossil evidence from 1.8 million to 400,000 years ago shows morphological diversity across regions, supporting the existence of multiple hominid species. These species, such as Homo erectus in Asia and Homo heidelbergensis in Africa and Europe, share ancestry with earlier African hominids but differ regionally. This pattern best supports the idea of multiple related, geographically separated species evolving from African ancestors.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
