      "generated_answer": "Castiglione emphasizes that the ideal courtier must excel in arms, possess physical prowess, be educated in the humanities, speak eloquently, understand music, and avoid vices like boasting. His vision centers on a well-rounded, elite male educated in both martial skills and the liberal arts, suggesting a focus on comprehensive, exclusive education for noble young men. The best fit is a private institution offering broad elite training, including academics, arts, and physical development.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
