    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{B}  \nThe boycott of foreign cloth was part of Gandhi's Swadeshi movement, which emphasized economic self-reliance and resistance to colonial exploitation\u2014similar to how the Columbian Exchange (initiated by Columbus\u2019s voyage) led to global trade networks that eventually enabled European colonial dominance, including in India. Gandhi sought to reverse the economic impact of such global trade imbalances by promoting indigenous production.",
