      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}  \nThe decline of both the Roman and Chinese empires led to more patriarchal social structures, reinforcing traditional gender roles. As centralized authority weakened, conservative norms emphasizing family hierarchy and female subordination became more pronounced. This resulted in a general decline in the rights of women during the post-classical period.",
