      "generated_answer": "The passage discusses non-alignment and cooperation with all states regardless of their economic system\u2014capitalist, socialist, or mixed\u2014reflecting the geopolitical context of the Cold War. Kwame Nkrumah, writing in 1965, refers to a policy of engaging with both Western and Eastern blocs without aligning with either, which was characteristic of the Cold War era. Therefore, the \"co-operation\" mentioned refers to navigating relations between the competing ideologies of the Cold War.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
