      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{D}  \nBeveridge argues that the United States has a moral obligation to civilize and uplift less developed peoples, portraying American rule as just and humane compared to indigenous or other foreign rule. He dismisses the need for consent from colonized peoples, asserting that governance should be guided by duty to civilization rather than self-determination. This reflects the imperialist ideology of the \"White Man's Burden.\"",
