      "generated_answer": "\\boxed{I}\n\nThe Great Depression that started in 1929 severely weakened the global economy, including British textile industries, making Indian self-reliance through swadeshi more viable. As foreign goods became less affordable and accessible, the boycott of British cloth gained greater traction among Indians. This economic pressure significantly boosted the success of Gandhi\u2019s call for boycotting foreign cloth and promoting spinning and weaving.",
