      "generated_answer": "The passage emphasizes human potential and freedom to choose one's nature, highlighting man's unique position among creatures due to divine generosity. Pico contrasts man\u2019s unlimited potential with the fixed natures of other beings, implying rejection of any belief in inherent limitations on human possibility. Therefore, the most logical inference is that Pico rejected the idea that man has limited potential.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
