      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef solve():\n    N, M = map(int, sys.stdin.readline().split())\n    S = sys.stdin.readline().strip()\n    \n    plain_tshirts = M\n    logo_needed = 0\n    current_logo_wearing = 0\n    max_consecutive_events = 0\n    consecutive_events = 0\n    \n    for c in S:\n        if c == '0':\n            # Wash all worn T-shirts\n            consecutive_events = 0\n        elif c == '1':\n            # Go out for a meal - can use plain or logo\n            if plain_tshirts > 0:\n                plain_tshirts -= 1\n            else:\n                current_logo_wearing += 1\n            consecutive_events = 0\n        elif c == '2':\n            # Attend competitive programming event - must use logo\n            current_logo_wearing += 1\n            consecutive_events += 1\n            max_consecutive_events = max(max_consecutive_events, consecutive_events)\n    \n    # The maximum number of logo shirts needed at once is the maximum consecutive events\n    # or when we run out of plain t-shirts for meals followed by events\n    result = max(0, current_logo_wearing - M)\n    # But we also need to consider washing cycles\n    result = max(result, max_consecutive_events)\n    \n    print(result)\n\nsolve()\n```",
