      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom collections import defaultdict, deque\n\ndef can_reach(graph, start, end, n):\n    if start == end:\n        return True\n    visited = [False] * (n + 1)\n    queue = deque([start])\n    visited[start] = True\n    \n    while queue:\n        node = queue.popleft()\n        for neighbor in graph[node]:\n            if neighbor == end:\n                return True\n            if not visited[neighbor]:\n                visited[neighbor] = True\n                queue.append(neighbor)\n    \n    return False\n\ndef solve():\n    n, m = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    edges = []\n    graph = defaultdict(list)\n    \n    for _ in range(m):\n        u, v = map(int, input().split())\n        edges.append((u, v))\n        if u != v:  # Ignore self-loops for connectivity\n            graph[u].append(v)\n            graph[v].append(u)\n    \n    k = int(input())\n    constraints = []\n    for _ in range(k):\n        x, y = map(int, input().split())\n        constraints.append((x, y))\n    \n    q = int(input())\n    \n    for _ in range(q):\n        p, q_vertex = map(int, input().split())\n        \n        # Create new graph with added edge\n        test_graph = defaultdict(list)\n        for u, v in edges:\n            if u != v:\n                test_graph[u].append(v)\n                test_graph[v].append(u)\n        \n        # Add the new edge\n        if p != q_vertex:\n            test_graph[p].append(q_vertex)\n            test_graph[q_vertex].append(p)\n        \n        # Check if all constraints are still satisfied\n        is_good = True\n        for x, y in constraints:\n            if can_reach(test_graph, x, y, n):\n                is_good = False\n                break\n        \n        print(\"Yes\" if is_good else \"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
