    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\nfrom heapq import heappush, heappop\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    idx = 0\n    N = int(data[idx])\n    M = int(data[idx + 1])\n    idx += 2\n    \n    edges = []\n    parent = list(range(N + 1))\n    \n    def find(x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find(parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx != ry:\n            parent[ry] = rx\n            return True\n        return False\n    \n    for _ in range(M):\n        K = int(data[idx])\n        C = int(data[idx + 1])\n        idx += 2\n        A = list(map(int, data[idx:idx + K]))\n        idx += K\n        \n        # Add edges for every pair in A\n        for i in range(K):\n            for j in range(i + 1, K):\n                u, v = A[i], A[j]\n                edges.append((C, u, v))\n                \n                # Use union-find to track connectivity during edge additions\n                union(u, v)\n    \n    # Check if the graph is connected\n    root = find(1)\n    for i in range(2, N + 1):\n        if find(i) != root:\n            print(-1)\n            return\n    \n    # Now compute MST using Kruskal's algorithm\n    edges.sort()\n    mst_weight = 0\n    parent = list(range(N + 1))\n    \n    def find_root(x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find_root(parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n    \n    for cost, u, v in edges:\n        if find_root(u) != find_root(v):\n            union(u, v)\n            mst_weight += cost\n    \n    print(mst_weight)\n\nmain()\n```",
