8\r\n\nIf cell (1,3) is repainted green, the number of green connected components becomes 1.\nIf cell (2,2) is repainted green, the number of green connected components becomes 1.\nIf cell (3,2) is repainted green, the number of green connected components becomes 2.\nIf cell (3,3) is repainted green, the number of green connected components becomes 2.\nTherefore, the expected value of the number of green connected components after choosing one red cell uniformly at random and repainting it green is (1+1+2+2)/4 = 3/2.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n4 5\r\n..#..\r\n.###.\r\n#####\r\n..#..\n\nSample Output 2\n\n598946613\n\nSample Input 3\n\n3 4\r\n#...\r\n.#.#\r\n..##\n\nSample Output 3\n\n285212675",
    "prediction": "claude-3-haiku-20240307",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nfrom collections import deque\n\nMOD = 998244353\n\ndef modinv(a, m=MOD):\n    return pow(a, m - 2, m)\n\ndef count_components(grid, H, W):\n    visited = [[False] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    count = 0\n    \n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '#' and not visited[i][j]:\n                # BFS to mark all cells in this component\n                queue = deque([(i, j)])\n                visited[i][j] = True\n                while queue:\n                    x, y = queue.popleft()\n                    for dx, dy in [(0, 1), (0, -1), (1, 0), (-1, 0)]:\n                        nx, ny = x + dx, y + dy\n                        if 0 <= nx < H and 0 <= ny < W and grid[nx][ny] == '#' and not visited[nx][ny]:\n                            visited[nx][ny] = True\n                            queue.append((nx, ny))\n                count += 1\n    \n    return count\n\ndef solve():\n    H, W = map(int, input().split())\n    grid = []\n    for _ in range(H):\n        grid.append(list(input().strip()))\n    \n    # Find all red cells\n    red_cells = []\n    for i in range(H):\n        for j in range(W):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                red_cells.append((i, j))\n    \n    total_components = 0\n    \n    # For each red cell, paint it green and count components\n    for i, j in red_cells:\n        grid[i][j] = '#'\n        components = count_components(grid, H, W)\n        total_components += components\n        grid[i][j] = '.'\n    \n    # Expected value = total_components / len(red_cells)\n    # We need to compute (total_components * modinv(len(red_cells))) % MOD\n    num_red = len(red_cells)\n    result = (total_components * modinv(num_red)) % MOD\n    \n    print(result)\n\nsolve()\n```",
