      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef minimum_time_to_revert(word: str, k: int) -> int:\n    n = len(word)\n    \n    # Try all possible times t (starting from 1)\n    for t in range(1, n + 1):\n        # After t operations, we have removed t*k characters\n        # So the remaining original string is word[t*k:] (if t*k < n)\n        # And we want this to match the original word, meaning:\n        # The string after t operations is word[t*k:] + (some k*t chars at end)\n        # For it to be equal to original word, we need word == word[t*k:] + ????\n        # That means word[0:n - t*k] must equal word[t*k: t*k + (n - t*k)] = word[t*k: n]\n        # i.e., word[0: n - t*k] == word[t*k: n]\n        \n        if t * k >= n:\n            # If we've removed more than or equal to the length, the entire original string is gone,\n            # and we can reconstruct anything, so it's always possible\n            return t\n        \n        # Check if word is periodic with period t*k\n        # Specifically, check if word[0:n - t*k] == word[t*k: n]\n        if word[:n - t*k] == word[t*k:]:\n            return t\n    \n    return n  # fallback\n```",
