tput 1\n\n3\r\n1 1 1 0 0 1 0 1\r\n\nThe sample output corresponds to the following actions:\n\n- Find potions of types 2,3,1 in this order. Pick up all of them.\n- Find potions of types 3,2 in this order. Do not pick up any of them.\n- Encounter a type-3 monster. Use one type-3 potion to defeat it.\n- Find a type-3 potion. Pick it up.\n- Find a type-3 potion. Do not pick it up.\n- Encounter a type-3 monster. Use one type-3 potion to defeat it.\n- Find a type-3 potion. Pick it up.\n- Encounter a type-2 monster. Use one type-2 potion to defeat it.\n- Encounter a type-3 monster. Use one type-3 potion to defeat it.\n- Encounter a type-1 monster. Use one type-1 potion to defeat it.\n\nIn this sequence of actions, the value of K is 3.\nThere is no way to avoid defeat with K\\leq 2, so the sought value of K _ {{\\min}} is 3.\r\nThere are multiple sequences of actions that satisfy K=3 and allow him to avoid defeat; you may print any of them.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n4\r\n2 3\r\n1 4\r\n2 1\r\n1 2\n\nSample Output 2\n\n-1\r\n\nHe will inevitably be defeated by the first monster he encounters.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n30\r\n1 25\r\n1 2\r\n1 10\r\n1 18\r\n2 18\r\n1 11\r\n2 11\r\n1 21\r\n1 6\r\n2 2\r\n2 10\r\n1 11\r\n1 24\r\n1 11\r\n1 3\r\n1 2\r\n1 18\r\n2 25\r\n1 8\r\n1 10\r\n1 11\r\n2 18\r\n2 10\r\n1 10\r\n2 2\r\n1 24\r\n1 10\r\n2 10\r\n1 25\r\n2 6\n\nSample Output 3\n\n4\r\n1 1 1 1 1 0 1 0 0 0 0 1 1 0 1 0 1 0 0 0",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    import sys\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    events = []\n    index = 1\n    for _ in range(n):\n        t = int(data[index])\n        x = int(data[index + 1])\n        index += 2\n        events.append((t, x))\n    \n    # Count required potions per type\n    potion_needed = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for t, x in events:\n        if t == 2:\n            potion_needed[x] += 1\n    \n    # Simulate forward: determine minimal pickup strategy\n    inventory = [0] * (n + 1)\n    max_potions = 0\n    current_potions = 0\n    pickups = []\n    \n    # We'll decide later which ones to pick up; first check feasibility\n    future_monsters = [0] * (n + 1)\n    for t, x in reversed(events):\n        if t == 2:\n            future_monsters[x] += 1\n    \n    can_defeat = True\n    for t, x in events:\n        if t == 1:\n            # Decide whether to pick up\n            if future_monsters[x] > 0:\n                pickups.append(1)\n                inventory[x] += 1\n                current_potions += 1\n                future_monsters[x] -= 1\n            else:\n                pickups.append(0)\n        else:  # t == 2\n            if inventory[x] <= 0:\n                can_defeat = False\n                break\n            inventory[x] -= 1\n        max_potions = max(max_potions, current_potions)\n    \n    if not can_defeat:\n        print(-1)\n        return\n    \n    # Now minimize the peak inventory (K_min)\n    # Use binary search on K_min\n    def can_succeed_with_limit(limit):\n        inv = [0] * (n + 1)\n        cur = 0\n        fut_mon = potion_needed[:]\n        for t, x in events:\n            if t == 1:\n                if fut_mon[x] > 0 and cur < limit:\n                    inv[x] += 1\n                    cur += 1\n                    fut_mon[x] -= 1\n            else:\n                if inv[x] <= 0:\n                    return False\n                inv[x] -= 1\n        return True\n\n    lo, hi = 0, n\n    K_min = n\n    while lo <= hi:\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        if can_succeed_with_limit(mid):\n            K_min = mid\n            hi = mid - 1\n        else:\n            lo = mid + 1\n    \n    # Reconstruct actions achieving K_min\n    inventory = [0] * (n + 1)\n    current = 0\n    future = potion_needed[:]\n    actions = []\n    for t, x in events:\n        if t == 1:\n            if future[x] > 0 and current < K_min:\n                inventory[x] += 1\n                current += 1\n                future[x] -= 1\n                actions.append(1)\n            else:\n                actions.append(0)\n        else:\n            inventory[x] -= 1\n    \n    print(K_min)\n    print(' '.join(map(str, [a for i, (t, x) in enumerate(events) if t == 1 for a in [actions[i]]])))\n\nmain()\n```",
