    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef countSubMultisets(nums, l, r):\n    MOD = 10**9 + 7\n    \n    # Count occurrences of each number\n    from collections import Counter\n    count = Counter(nums)\n    \n    # Total sum of all elements\n    total_sum = sum(nums)\n    \n    # dp[i] = number of sub-multisets with sum i\n    dp = [0] * (total_sum + 1)\n    dp[0] = 1  # empty multiset\n    \n    # For each unique number and its count\n    for num, freq in sorted(count.items()):\n        # Traverse from right to left to avoid using same element multiple times in one iteration\n        for s in range(total_sum, num - 1, -1):\n            # For each occurrence of this number\n            for k in range(1, freq + 1):\n                if s - k * num >= 0:\n                    dp[s] = (dp[s] + dp[s - k * num]) % MOD\n    \n    # Sum up all sub-multisets with sum in range [l, r]\n    result = sum(dp[l:r+1]) % MOD\n    return result\n```",
