      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    n, h, w = map(int, input().split())\n    tiles = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        tiles.append(tuple(map(int, input().split())))\n\n    target_area = h * w\n\n    import itertools\n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        current_area = 0\n        selected_tiles = []\n        for j in range(n):\n            if (i >> j) & 1:\n                selected_tiles.append(tiles[j])\n\n        possible = False\n        \n        \n        for rotations in itertools.product([0,1], repeat = len(selected_tiles)):\n          \n          current_area = 0\n          for k in range(len(selected_tiles)):\n            tile = selected_tiles[k]\n            \n            if rotations[k] == 0:\n              current_area += tile[0] * tile[1]\n            \n            else:\n              current_area += tile[1] * tile[0]\n          \n          if current_area == target_area:\n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            valid = True\n            for k in range(len(selected_tiles)):\n              tile = selected_tiles[k]\n              if rotations[k] == 0:\n                \n                if (tile[0] > h or tile[1] > w) and (tile[0] > w or tile[1] > h):\n                  valid = False\n                  \n                \n              else:\n              \n                if (tile[1] > h or tile[0] > w) and (tile[1] > w or tile[0] > h):\n                  valid = False\n            if valid:              \n              possible = True\n              break\n        \n        \n        if possible:\n          print(\"Yes\")\n          return\n\n    print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
