      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    N, H, W = map(int, input().split())\n    tiles = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        a, b = map(int, input().split())\n        tiles.append((a, b))\n    \n    target_area = H * W\n    \n    def can_place(grid, tile_idx, tiles_used):\n        # Find first uncovered cell\n        uncovered = None\n        for i in range(H):\n            for j in range(W):\n                if grid[i][j] == -1:\n                    uncovered = (i, j)\n                    break\n            if uncovered:\n                break\n        \n        # All cells covered\n        if uncovered is None:\n            return True\n        \n        r, c = uncovered\n        \n        # Try each unused tile\n        for idx in range(N):\n            if idx in tiles_used:\n                continue\n            \n            a, b = tiles[idx]\n            \n            # Try both orientations\n            for h, w in [(a, b), (b, a)]:\n                # Try to place at (r, c)\n                if r + h <= H and c + w <= W:\n                    # Check if all cells in rectangle are uncovered\n                    valid = True\n                    for i in range(r, r + h):\n                        for j in range(c, c + w):\n                            if grid[i][j] != -1:\n                                valid = False\n                                break\n                        if not valid:\n                            break\n                    \n                    if valid:\n                        # Place tile\n                        for i in range(r, r + h):\n                            for j in range(c, c + w):\n                                grid[i][j] = idx\n                        \n                        tiles_used.add(idx)\n                        \n                        if can_place(grid, tile_idx + 1, tiles_used):\n                            return True\n                        \n                        # Remove tile\n                        tiles_used.remove(idx)\n                        for i in range(r, r + h):\n                            for j in range(c, c + w):\n                                grid[i][j] = -1\n        \n        return False\n    \n    grid = [[-1] * W for _ in range(H)]\n    if can_place(grid, 0, set()):\n        print(\"Yes\")\n    else:\n        print(\"No\")\n\nsolve()\n```",
