    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef findMissingAndRepeatedValues(grid):\n    n = len(grid)\n    total_elements = n * n\n    seen = set()\n    repeated = None\n    missing = None\n    \n    # Flatten the grid and find the repeated number\n    for row in grid:\n        for num in row:\n            if num in seen:\n                repeated = num\n            else:\n                seen.add(num)\n    \n    # Find the missing number by checking expected sum vs actual sum\n    expected_sum = total_elements * (total_elements + 1) // 2\n    actual_sum = sum(sum(row) for row in grid)\n    \n    # The difference between expected and actual sum gives us (missing - repeated)\n    missing = expected_sum - actual_sum + repeated\n    \n    return [repeated, missing]\n```",
