      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef canTraverseAllPairs(nums):\n    n = len(nums)\n    if n == 1:\n        return True\n    \n    # Remove duplicates and handle edge case with single element\n    nums = list(set(nums))\n    n = len(nums)\n    \n    # If there's a 1, it cannot connect to any other number since gcd(1, x) = 1\n    if 1 in nums:\n        return n == 1\n    \n    # Union-Find data structure\n    parent = list(range(n))\n    rank = [0] * n\n    \n    def find(x):\n        if parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = find(parent[x])\n        return parent[x]\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        px, py = find(x), find(y)\n        if px == py:\n            return\n        if rank[px] < rank[py]:\n            px, py = py, px\n        parent[py] = px\n        if rank[px] == rank[py]:\n            rank[px] += 1\n    \n    # For each number, factorize and group indices by prime factors\n    prime_to_indices = {}\n    for i, num in enumerate(nums):\n        d = 2\n        temp = num\n        while d * d <= temp:\n            if temp % d == 0:\n                while temp % d == 0:\n                    temp //= d\n                if d not in prime_to_indices:\n                    prime_to_indices[d] = []\n                prime_to_indices[d].append(i)\n            d += 1\n        if temp > 1:\n            if temp not in prime_to_indices:\n                prime_to_indices[temp] = []\n            prime_to_indices[temp].append(i)\n    \n    # Union all indices sharing the same prime factor\n    for indices in prime_to_indices.values():\n        for j in range(1, len(indices)):\n            union(indices[0], indices[j])\n    \n    # Check if all indices are connected\n    root = find(0)\n    return all(find(i) == root for i in range(1, n))\n```",
