    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().splitlines()\n    \n    H, W, N = map(int, data[0].split())\n    T = data[1].strip()\n    grid = [line.strip() for line in data[2:2+H]]\n    \n    possible_positions = set()\n    \n    for i in range(1, H - 1):\n        for j in range(1, W - 1):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                r, c = i, j\n                valid = True\n                for move in T:\n                    if move == 'L':\n                        c -= 1\n                    elif move == 'R':\n                        c += 1\n                    elif move == 'U':\n                        r -= 1\n                    elif move == 'D':\n                        r += 1\n                    if grid[r][c] == '#':\n                        valid = False\n                        break\n                if valid:\n                    possible_positions.add((r, c))\n    \n    print(len(possible_positions))\n\nmain()\n```",
