      "generated_answer": "```python\ndef solve():\n    H, W, N = map(int, input().split())\n    T = input().strip()\n    grid = []\n    for _ in range(H):\n        grid.append(input().strip())\n    \n    # Direction mappings\n    directions = {\n        'L': (0, -1),\n        'R': (0, 1),\n        'U': (-1, 0),\n        'D': (1, 0)\n    }\n    \n    # Find all possible starting positions\n    possible_starts = set()\n    \n    # Try each cell as a potential starting position\n    for start_i in range(H):\n        for start_j in range(W):\n            if grid[start_i][start_j] == '#':\n                continue\n            \n            # Simulate the path from this starting position\n            i, j = start_i, start_j\n            valid = True\n            \n            for move in T:\n                di, dj = directions[move]\n                ni, nj = i + di, j + dj\n                \n                # Check if new position is within bounds and is land\n                if 0 <= ni < H and 0 <= nj < W and grid[ni][nj] == '.':\n                    i, j = ni, nj\n                else:\n                    valid = False\n                    break\n            \n            if valid:\n                possible_starts.add((i, j))\n    \n    print(len(possible_starts))\n\nsolve()\n```",
