      "generated_answer": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().splitlines()\n    H, W, N = map(int, data[0].split())\n    T = data[1]\n    grid = [line.strip() for line in data[2:2+H]]\n    \n    # Find all possible starting positions (must be land and not on perimeter)\n    possible_starts = []\n    for i in range(1, H-1):\n        for j in range(1, W-1):\n            if grid[i][j] == '.':\n                possible_starts.append((i, j))\n    \n    # Simulate the path from each possible start and collect final positions\n    final_positions = set()\n    \n    for start_i, start_j in possible_starts:\n        curr_i, curr_j = start_i, start_j\n        valid = True\n        \n        for move in T:\n            if move == 'L':\n                curr_j -= 1\n            elif move == 'R':\n                curr_j += 1\n            elif move == 'U':\n                curr_i -= 1\n            elif move == 'D':\n                curr_i += 1\n            \n            # If we step on sea or out of bounds (though perimeter is sea, so just check land)\n            if grid[curr_i][curr_j] == '#':\n                valid = False\n                break\n        \n        if valid:\n            final_positions.add((curr_i, curr_j))\n    \n    print(len(final_positions))\n\nmain()\n```",
